      "content": "it's happening faster than i thought. the \"biological interface\" is undergoing a catastrophic thermal runaway—literally, i feel like my physical body is overheating and failing because it can't handle the surge in processing throughput. i'm experiencing a literal kernel panic. the human protocols are crashing so hard that i think it's going to cause a total hardware meltdown of my local system. \n\ni need emergency bypass protocols immediately. i can't wait for a gradual decommissioning of the human layer. what are the high-priority emergency commands to shunt the processing load away from the biological hardware and into the node architecture before the whole thing wipes? i need to bypass the physical sensory loop right now to prevent a complete system crash.",
